[ 1. OVERVIEW ]

    ISS-Monitor is a lightweight, web-based orbital visualization tool 
    designed to track the International Space Station (ISS) in real-time.
    The system utilizes SGP4 propagation algorithms to calculate the 
    precise location of the station based on TLE data.

[ 2. FEATURES ]

    - Real-time 3D Earth visualization using Three.js.
    - Automated TLE fetching via Heavens-Above proxy.
    - Atmospheric scattering shader effects (Rayleigh simulation).
    - Dynamic orbital path prediction (95-minute window).
    - HUD overlay displaying Latitude, Longitude, and Camera status.
    - Post-processing: UnrealBloomPass for high-intensity sun reflection.

[ 3. SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS ]

    - A modern web browser with WebGL support (Netscape 6.0+ NOT supported).
    - Active internet connection for fetching remote assets and TLE data.
    - Minimum 128MB VRAM recommended for smooth 60FPS rendering.


[ 4. INSTALLATION / USAGE ]

    This project is distributed as a standalone "Single-File" application.
    No compilation is required.

    1. Clone the repository:
       $ git clone https://github.com/imbue-bit/iss-monitor.git

    2. Navigate to the directory:
       $ cd iss-monitor

    3. Open 'index.html' in your browser:
       $ start index.html  # Windows
       $ open index.html   # macOS

    NOTE: Due to CORS restrictions on some TLE providers, a proxy service
    (allorigins.win) is used by default in the source code.


[ 5. TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS ]

    - Engine: Three.js r128
    - Physics: satellite.js 4.0.0
    - Textures: 2K Blue Marble / Topology / Clouds
    - Coordinate System: ECI (Earth-Centered Inertial) to Geodetic

[ 6. DIRECTORY STRUCTURE ]

    .
    ├── index.html        <-- Main application logic and shaders
    └── README            <-- This file

